  "body_markdown": "About us\n\nmeet Dr. ChrisMeet The TeamLivewell DifferenceOffice TourTechnologyJoin Our Team\n\nservices\n\ndCOEFull Mouth ReconstructionSedation Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nSmile MakeoverPorcelain VeneersNo Prep VeneersGum RecontouringTeeth WhiteningDental Bonding\n\nImplant Dentistry\n\nDental ImplantsSingle ImplantsImplant BridgesAll-on-X ImplantsLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nDental CrownsInlays & OnlaysDental BridgesTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone GraftingRidge AugmentationTooth ExtractionSinus LiftWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nOrthodontics\n\nInvisalignBraces\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPreventive DentistryPreventive CleaningGum TherapyRoot Canal Therapy\n\nTMJ TreatmentDental Emergencies\n\nnew patient\n\nfirst visit & new examInsurance & FinancingBlog\n\nOur work\n\nSmile GalleryTestimonials\n\nContact\n\ncall (703) 690-0102Request An Appointment\n\nBook Now\n\n703-690-0102\n\nLivewell Difference\n\nmeet Dr. Chris\n\nMeet The Team\n\nJoin Our Team\n\nOffice Tour\n\nTechnology\n\nServices\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nDCOE\n\nTMJ Treatment\n\nDental Emergencies\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPreventive\n\nDental Bridges\n\nRoot Canal\n\nProfessional Dental Cleaning\n\nScaling & Root Planing\n\nAll General Dentistry services\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nNo Prep Veneers\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nGum Recontouring\n\nAll Cosmetic Dentistry Services\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Bridges\n\nAll-on-X Implants\n\nLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nAll Implant Dentistry Services\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nTooth Extraction\n\nSinus Lift\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nInvisalign\n\nBraces\n\nAll Orthodontics Services\n\nDental Crowns\n\nTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nDental Bonding\n\nInlays & Onlays\n\nAll Restorative Dentistry Services\n\nNew Patient\n\nfirst visit & new exam\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nBlog\n\nTestimonials\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nCALL US: (703) 690-0102\n\nBOOK AN APPOINTMENT\n\n320+\n\n5 Star Reviews\n\n\n# Wisdom Teeth Removal in Fairfax Station, VA\n\n\n\n## What Is Wisdom Teeth Removal?\n\n\nWisdom teeth are the last molars to develop, usually in the late teens or early twenties. For some people, they grow in normally. For many others, there simply is not enough room.\n\nWhen wisdom teeth are trapped under the gums, angled toward other teeth, or only partly erupted, they can lead to pain, swelling, cavities, gum infection, and pressure in the jaw.\n\nWisdom teeth removal is a planned procedure that removes these teeth before they create bigger problems. The goal is to protect your comfort, your bite, and the health of the teeth around them.\n\n\n## When Should Wisdom Teeth Be Checked?\n\n\nYou may benefit from an evaluation if you notice:\n\nPressure or soreness in the back of the mouth\n\n‍A dull ache near the jaw, gums, or back molars can be a sign that wisdom teeth are pushing or trapped.\n\nSwollen or irritated gums\n\n‍Partially erupted wisdom teeth can be hard to clean, which may lead to inflammation or infection.\n\nCrowding or shifting teeth\n\n‍Wisdom teeth can sometimes place pressure on nearby teeth, especially when space is limited.\n\nFood trapping behind the molars\n\n‍When wisdom teeth are partly visible, the area can collect bacteria and become difficult to keep clean.\n\n\n## Benefits of Wisdom Teeth Removal\n\n\n\n### Prevents Pain and Infection\n\n\nRemoving problem wisdom teeth can help stop recurring swelling, gum irritation, and jaw discomfort.\n\n\n### Protects Surrounding Teeth\n\n\nWisdom teeth can damage nearby molars or create areas that are difficult to clean. Removal helps protect those teeth.\n\n\n### Reduces Risk of Future Complications\n\n\nEarly evaluation and timely removal can make treatment simpler before pain, infection, or cysts develop.\n\n\n## The Wisdom Teeth Removal Process\n\n\nEvaluate. Plan. Remove carefully\n\nExam & Digital Imaging\n\nWe take a close look at your wisdom teeth, their position, root shape, and relationship to nearby structures.\n\nA Clear Recommendation\n\nDr. Chris explains whether removal is needed now, can be monitored, or should be planned before symptoms get worse.\n\nComfort Planning\n\nWe review what to expect during the visit, how we will keep you comfortable, and how to prepare before your appointment.\n\nGentle Tooth Removal\n\nThe wisdom teeth are removed using a careful approach based on their position, whether they are erupted, partially erupted, or impacted.\n\nRecovery Instructions & Follow-Up\n\nYou receive clear home-care steps for swelling, food choices, cleaning, and healing so recovery feels easier to manage.\n\n\n## Wisdom Teeth Care That Feels Clear, Calm, and Planned\n\n\nWisdom teeth removal can feel intimidating, especially if you are already in pain or nervous about surgery. At Livewell Dental, we slow the process down, explain what we see, and help you understand the safest path forward.\n\nWe do not recommend removal just because wisdom teeth exist. We look at your symptoms, imaging, age, tooth position, and risk for future problems before creating a plan.\n\nWhy patients choose Livewell:\n\nDigital imaging to understand tooth position clearly\n\nHonest guidance about whether removal is needed\n\nComfort-focused care for anxious patients\n\nSimple recovery instructions before you leave\n\nA team that explains every step without rushing you\n\nMEET DR. CHRIS\n\n\n## Trusted by Patients Who Want a Better Surgical Experience\n\n\nPatients choose Livewell Dental because they want to feel informed before making decisions. Wisdom teeth treatment is not just about removing teeth. It is about preventing future pain, protecting nearby molars, and helping you recover with confidence.\n\nFrom the first scan to the final recovery instructions, our team is here to make the experience feel more manageable, personal, and clear.\n\nSchedule a Consultation\n\nDo all wisdom teeth need to be removed?\n\nNo. Some wisdom teeth can stay if they are healthy, fully erupted, easy to clean, and not causing problems. We recommend removal when they are painful, impacted, infected, or likely to harm nearby teeth.\n\nWhat does impacted wisdom tooth mean?\n\nAn impacted wisdom tooth is trapped under the gums or bone, or angled in a way that prevents it from coming in properly.\n\nWhen is the best age to remove wisdom teeth?\n\nMany people are evaluated in their teens or early twenties because the roots may be easier to manage before they fully develop. Adults can still have wisdom teeth removed when needed.\n\nDoes wisdom teeth removal hurt?\n\nThe area is numbed during treatment, and we focus on keeping you comfortable. Soreness, swelling, and jaw stiffness are common afterward, but they usually improve as healing progresses.\n\nHow long does recovery take?\n\nMost patients feel significantly better within a few days, though full healing takes longer. We will give you instructions for food, cleaning, swelling, and activity.\n\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions About Wisdom Teeth Removal\n\n\nQuestions answered before you come in.\n\n\n### Reimagine your dental experience\n\n\n\n### address\n\n\n9027 Silverbrook Rd Ste. F\n\nFairfax Station, VA 22039\n\n\n### Contact\n\n\n\n### Hours\n\n\nMon-Tue: 8am-5pm\n\nWed-Thu: 8am-4pm\n\nFri: 8am-1pm\n\n\n### Connect\n\n\nServing Fairfax Station and the Greater Northern Virginia Area\n\nCopyright © TEXT-YEAR Livewell Dental\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms of Service\n\nCookie Policy\n\nHIPAA Disclosure\n\nConsent Preferences",
